---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About · Marcus J. Yoo"
  description="Mechanical engineering student at Rose-Hulman. Product design, fabrication, and a life built around climbing."
>
  <article class="prose narrow container">
    <header class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Marcus J. Yoo</h1>
      <p class="dek">
        Mechanical engineering student at Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology.
        I design and build physical things, and I care about the process as much
        as the result.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <p>
        I'm a junior mechanical engineering student, and I'm looking for a 
        <strong> Summer 2027 internship or a Spring/Summer co-op</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        I treat design as a complementary discipline to engineering, it
        sharpens how I think, how I communicate ideas visually, and how I bring
        a creative edge to technical work. The projects I care about most are
        the ones where the process is as interesting as the outcome, where you
        can trace every decision from a constraint, a calculation, or a failed
        prototype.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What I work on</h2>
      <p>
        My main project right now is the <a href="/projects/pcbrule/">PCBrule</a>,
        a slide rule made from printed circuit board. What started as a
        "wouldn't it be cool if" idea in high school has turned into real product
        development mechanical design, GD&T, PCB layout, prototyping, and the
        messy iteration in between.
      </p>
      <p>
        Other work includes a removable fin attachment system for NASA USLI, a
        DIY snowskate built from a recycled kids' ski with waterjet-cut mounting
        plates, and an ESP32-based finger strength trainer for climbing. I also
        interned at Boeing in flight performance engineering, developing tools
        to analyze large-scale simulation data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Outside of engineering</h2>
      <p>
        Climbing is a big part of my life. I don't see a version of my future
        that doesn't include it in some way. The outdoors is where I reset, and
        climbing is how I stay connected to it. I think it would be really awesome to work someplace who specializes in a field adjacent to climbing or the outdoors. I plan on getting both IRATA and SPRAT rope access certifications.
      </p>
      <p>
        I like to write, both as a way of thinking through problems and as a way
        of documenting what I'm working on. I'm involved with the Rose-Hulman
        chapter of the Young Democratic Socialists of America, where I
        co-founded the chapter and serve as Vice Chair. I think it's important, more than ever, to make an effort to understand what's happening in
        the world at large, and to have the language to talk about it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="contact">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        The best way to reach me is
        <a href={`mailto:${site.author.email}`}>{site.author.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .container { max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 5rem 1.5rem; }

  .head { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .head h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    line-height: .95;
    letter-spacing: -.05em;
    margin: .5rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .dek {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin: 0;
  }

  section { margin-top: 3rem; }
  section h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    letter-spacing: -.01em;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  strong { font-weight: 600; }
  a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .contact { margin-top: 4rem; padding-top: 3rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
</style>